Z||000021||Mach10||08-31-2001||01:13 AM||||On the contrary. I'm studying forensics. Blood and guts don't bother me. Does the smell of rotting human flesh bother you? How about plane crash victims? Burnt corpses? How about the skeleton of a 12 year old girl with an axe blade stuck in her forehead? Does that idea offend you? I've gotten somewhat desensitized to these things. They don't bother me so much anymore. The fact that this man is pandering to the bloodlust of society does. <P>While I'll admit that the cliff vs. legs argument swings between two extremes, I still think that this guy is an idiot. There are much better ways of raising the necessary cash than adding to the reeking stack of collectible human misery.<P>Read his articles. He *can* walk right now. That's why the insurance company won't pay for his new feet. I agree that the insurance company is wrong. It's not about neccessary/unnecessary surgery, it's about quality of life. He WOULD be better off without his feet. But it should not be this way.<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 08-31-2001).]||||reg||3
